    "content": "Eid prayer (Salat al-Eid) is typically held in the morning, shortly after sunrise (roughly 7:00 AM to 10:30 AM local time), depending on the local mosque or community, and lasts until noon. Common times are between 8:30 AM and 9:30 AM, with many mosques offering multiple, staggered prayer times to accommodate worshippers. Key Details on Eid Prayer Times (March 2026): Optimal Timing: The prayer occurs after sunrise but before the Dhuhr (noon) prayer. Common Locations: Prayers are held at local mosques (like the ADAMS Center or Diyanet Center of America) or designated outdoor community grounds (Eidgah). ADAMS Center Diyanet Center of America Regional Examples (March 2026): Columbus, OH: 8:30 a.m., 9:30 a.m., and 10:30 a.m.. Dubai: 6:40 a.m.. London: Often 9:00 AM - 10:00 AM. Preparation: It is Sunnah (tradition) to take a ghusl (shower) before the prayer and eat an odd number of dates beforehand. Note: It is highly recommended to check with your local mosque for specific prayer times, as they can vary.",
